is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router6
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Router6’s Linux firewall (netfilter/iptables) in the forwarding path. Mechanism: Inter-site traffic from the transit link is being dropped by FORWARD chain rules on router6, so hosts in 172.16.10.0/24 can reach router6’s interfaces but not the end hosts behind it.

Evidence and localization:
- From PC4/PC5, pings to Location C hosts (e.g., 172.18.51.15) time out, but pings to router6’s interfaces 172.18.50.254 and 172.18.51.254 succeed, proving L3 reachability to router6 and failure only for forwarded traffic.
- Router0 has correct RIP routes toward 172.18.51.0/24 via 10.16.1.2, and router6 itself can ping 172.18.51.15 successfully, isolating the issue to router6’s forwarding path, not routing.
-
